      "content": "You're absolutely right to question that, and I agree that a strict income-only approach is often more equitable for the most vulnerable populations who are currently priced out of transit-rich areas. However, I believe the best solution is a hybrid model that prioritizes transit access as the primary driver because it actively breaks the cycle of poverty by connecting people to jobs and education, whereas income-only allocation often leaves them stuck in dead-end neighborhoods. We should use income criteria as a strict eligibility floor to ensure the poorest are included, but the distribution logic must favor mobility to truly solve the affordability crisis.",
